dialogue trust_engineer_5
title: Question four
trigger: Trust engineer level=5
once
speaker commander $commander
speaker hero $with

node open commander
  The Engineer sits on the wagon's tailboard with the grease-black notebook open across both knees. It is nearly full. The last written page has only one line on it.
  * Did the orb ever tell you anything, after I let you open it? -> lent_back
    if: FlagSet engineer:orb_lent
    do: AddTrust $with 5
  * Still measuring me? The gauge must be worn out by now. -> watched_back
    if: FlagSet engineer:orb_watched
    do: AddTrust $with 5
  * I told you to leave the orb be. You did. I never thanked you for that. -> refused_back
    if: FlagSet engineer:orb_refused
    do: AddTrust $with 7
  * That notebook's nearly done. -> notebook
    do: AddTrust $with 3

node lent_back hero
  It told me it was put together by people who never expected anyone else to open it. Every screw was a bit rude about it. I put them all back. Sit down.
  -> seal

node watched_back hero
  The gauge is fine. The needle's bent toward you permanently. I've stopped trying to straighten it. Sit down.
  -> seal

node refused_back hero
  I was annoyed for a month. Then I watched what you do with it in a fight, and I stopped. Sit down.
  -> seal

node notebook hero
  Nearly. I've been saving the last page. Sit down.
  -> seal

node seal hero
  Answers first. I worked out Tap Seven. Not what shut it. I still don't know that. But I worked out that the seal didn't fail. It closed, clean, the way it was built to. Nothing I did with a wrench could have made it do that, or stopped it.
  -> weight

node weight commander
  The Engineer says it twice more under the breath, as though checking the sum, and then looks up.
  * Then there was never any debt. We'll walk into the fish market and say so, together. -> shared_kept
    if: FlagSet engineer:debt_shared
    do: AddTrust $with 9
    do: SetFlag engineer:thread_together
  * I said Redline gets nothing. Now you can prove it. -> defied_kept
    if: FlagSet engineer:debt_defied
    do: AddTrust $with 8
    do: SetFlag engineer:thread_proved
  * I told you that debt was yours to settle. I was wrong. It was never yours, and it was never only yours to carry. -> sent_mended
    if: FlagSet engineer:debt_sent
    do: AddTrust $with 10
    do: SetFlag engineer:thread_mended
  * Then put it down. You've carried it long enough. -> put_down
    do: AddTrust $with 6
    do: SetFlag engineer:thread_free

node shared_kept hero
  Together. You've said it twice now. I think that makes it a contract. Redline is going to hate the look of us.
  -> last_page

node defied_kept hero
  I can. With numbers. Redline respects numbers more than it respects anyone. I'll write it up so even a ganger can follow it.
  -> last_page

node sent_mended hero
  You didn't have to say that. You did anyway. That's worth more to me than the sum on the paper ever was.
  -> last_page

node put_down hero
  Put it down. Huh. I've been holding it so long my hand's shaped round it. Give me a while. I'll get there.
  -> last_page

node last_page hero
  So. Question four. I wrote it down the night you found me in the red, and I've never been able to answer it with a gauge. Why did you stop the wagon?
  -> ask

node ask commander
  The Engineer turns the notebook round so the Commander can read the one line, and holds out the pencil.
  * Because you asked us not to run you down. Nobody else out there was asking for anything. -> asked
    do: AddTrust $with 8
    do: SetFlag engineer:list_asked
  * Because the axle was cracked, and I needed someone who'd notice. -> axle
    do: AddTrust $with 5
    do: SetFlag engineer:list_axle
  * I don't know. I'm not sure I could tell you why I do most things. -> unknown
    do: AddTrust $with -2
    do: SetFlag engineer:list_open

node asked hero
  Because I asked. Not because I was useful. I'm going to write that down exactly the way you said it, and then I'm going to start a new notebook.

node axle hero
  Ha. Useful, then. Fine. I'll take useful from you. You're the first one who ever said it to my face instead of paying me in blessings. Question five can wait.

node unknown hero
  Then it stays a question. That's all right. Some of the best parts I own, I still can't say what they do. I'll leave the page open, Commander. You can fill it in when you know.
